1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,280
Greetings, Sir Trillram. My landing castle is about to go dark, so this transmission will be terminated soon.

2
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:14,760
So let's wrap this up quickly. Have you taken care of our little rat problem?

3
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:24,720
Are you awake?

4
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:29,400
Oh, no you don't. We need to keep you here in bed.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,040
Where am I?

6
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:39,240
We're at the school for now. The Martians haven't figured out that we're here yet. We've stayed out of sight pretty well so far.

7
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,160
And what about the others?

8
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,400
You mean Inaho and his friends?

9
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:48,080
They say they're going to fight.

10
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,840
Using the equipment here.

11
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,960
Against the Martian cataphract.

12
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:56,060
Without the clock.

13
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,540
I Weihnfaced.

14
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:01,040
You shouldn't.

15
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,040
Oh

16
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,040
Oh

17
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:03,040
Oh

18
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:33,040
What the hell's going on here

19
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:34,900
Orders from headquarters, sir

20
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:39,340
We will be abandoning this base as soon as all the remaining citizens have been evacuated

21
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:41,740
We've still got an active unit out in combat

22
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:44,500
You're this area's only surviving fighter

23
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,740
Lieutenant Koichiro Marito

24
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:50,260
And you would be?

25
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,180
Darzana Mogberech

26
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,260
With the 4th Fleet Escort Force

27
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:56,900
CO Watatsumi Amphib Assault Ship

28
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,940
This is my XO, Kaoru Mizusaki

29
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:03,680
One of our people is still out there fighting

30
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:07,260
The only reason we're still secure here is because she's holding them off

31
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:08,100
Who is she?

32
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,980
Warrant officer Yuki Kaisuka

33
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:14,060
An EM field is damping radio signals around Shinowara

34
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:16,000
GPS is down too

35
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,980
Even if we tried to rescue her, we don't know her location

36
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:20,280
But Captain Chi

37
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:24,240
Our orders are to escort and protect refugees evacuating by ferry

38
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:27,040
But there are still people who haven't made it out yet

39
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,820
I didn't see my kids' names in the passenger manifest

40
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:32,060
They're my students

41
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:35,720
All right then

42
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:39,000
I'll submit a request to put together a rescue party for you

43
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,780
I can only leave you a single landing craft

44
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:46,060
However, if you can't assemble enough people to be her crew

45
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:48,200
Then you'll have to just forget about it

46
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,240
I'm sorry

47
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:53,920
Now! You're in there still, right?

48
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,340
Answer me! Now!

49
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:56,260
Occupied

50
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:58,100
I know that! That's why I'm knocking!

51
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:01,560
Do you have the slightest idea what you're all getting yourselves into?

52
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,260
I'm perfectly aware that it seems insane

53
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:05,660
Then why are you doing it?

54
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,780
We don't know why

55
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:10,340
But that Martian seems quite obsessed with trying to kill us

56
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:12,440
But as long as we're at the school

57
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:15,900
His attacks won't hit the harbor or the city either

58
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:19,180
Luckily, they evacuated everyone who lives around here

59
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,260
That doesn't mean you

60
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:29,220
And he killed Okisuke

61
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,060
Be more flexible

62
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,180
Look at things and make the call

63
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:35,460
Go with your gut

64
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:37,980
Isn't that what you always tell me, Yuki?

65
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:44,140
I think that it applies most right now

66
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:46,060
Then let me take care of it

67
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:47,940
You can't do it injured, Yuki

68
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:49,160
You're so stubborn

69
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:53,020
Everyone is affected by this

70
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:56,920
That's why I want you to be the one to comfort them

71
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:59,560
You can be here to cheer up the sad

72
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,400
And to reassure the frightened

73
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:05,380
After all, we students aren't capable of it

74
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:08,840
Princess

75
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:12,300
You desired peace more than anyone

76
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:16,720
Who would do this?

77
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:21,960
So you are saying that not only did you fail to kill the rat

78
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:24,720
You've lost track of where she's gone to ground?

79
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,200
With great respect, my lord Sosbaum

80
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:31,220
This elusive rat has only managed to delay the inevitable

81
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:32,600
And?

82
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:36,340
The tunnel used for escape only leads to one area

83
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:39,660
Shinawara's northernmost district

84
00:05:39,660 --> 00:05:43,660
When she impatiently pokes her little head up for a look

85
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:47,260
My Nilo Keras' eagle eyes will immediately spot her

86
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:48,320
You are a fool

87
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:51,860
Do you think we have the luxury of playing a waiting game?

88
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:55,460
If we do not have the rat's exact location

89
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:58,900
We shall simply turn the entire city to dust

90
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:02,880
We'll use meteors to bombard them

91
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:04,560
But, my lord Sosbaum

92
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:08,820
Count Cruteo's landing castle may be positioned too close for that

93
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:11,580
He may have the impression that he is being attacked

94
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,180
Collateral damages

95
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:15,980
Orbital corrections will take several hours

96
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:18,980
To ensure the rat does not flee elsewhere in the meantime

97
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:20,780
Maintain a close watch

98
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:21,740
Yes, my lord

99
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:24,360
What's that?

100
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,860
It's the Mars cataphract data I've collected

101
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:28,060
It's very interesting

102
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:36,540
The bullets you fired at it didn't bounce off

103
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,800
They were all absorbed, weren't they?

104
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,900
How's the signal for you?

105
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:45,240
Not that great

106
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:49,800
The impudence

107
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:51,580
And now

108
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:56,700
It's not just ammunition

109
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,340
Sensor pings hit it

110
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:00,060
But there are no return signals

111
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:02,180
And that means what?

112
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:05,020
Infrared, acoustical, lasers

113
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,300
They're all useless

114
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:09,720
Not so much as an echo comes back

115
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,700
It seems to be absorbing everything

116
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:14,260
From radio waves to even kinetic energy

117
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:16,020
That is the key part

118
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:18,160
The wall's special characteristic

119
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,200
The wall?

120
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:23,700
The cataphract's energy field covering its entire surface

121
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:25,660
You could call it a barrier, I guess

122
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:27,040
A barrier?

123
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:27,980
Yeah

124
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:30,920
A barrier that absorbs anything coming at it

125
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:33,900
Matter, sound, EMF, all of it

126
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,420
But then

127
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:38,400
If that's the case, how can he still see us?

128
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:41,240
Through the barrier, nothing should be visible to him

129
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:41,880
Huh?

130
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:45,620
All information from the outside is blocked by the barrier

131
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:51,440
Therefore, it's logical to assume he can't actually see or hear anything on this side of it

132
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:55,720
The data we've gathered so far says that the inside

133
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:58,840
Appears to be completely black

134
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:02,380
Wait, so then how does he target us so accurately?

135
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:03,560
Yeah, you're right

136
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:06,680
How can he hit anything if he wasn't even able to see it?

137
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:08,320
You remember?

138
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:12,440
He was able to target us precisely from the other side of a building

139
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:16,180
But then

140
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:19,040
Though he was almost right on top of us

141
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:22,140
He gave up the chase the instant we went into the tunnel

142
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:27,400
I would bet

143
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,580
He wasn't the one that was watching everything around him

144
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:34,180
I think that he's using another camera system

145
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:36,380
To feed him the visuals

146
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:39,220
Most likely some kind of high-level drone

147
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:41,220
Kind of like this

148
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:45,880
And so that was how he was able to stay on us no matter where we ran

149
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:48,240
And why he didn't follow us in the tunnel

150
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:52,700
He can't see anything for himself when that barrier is up

151
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:57,700
He's probably searching for us right now from overhead

152
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,120
That makes sense

153
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:04,440
And that means we'll be safe just as long as we stay undercover like we are now

154
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:08,040
Yes, but the moment we go out again, he'll spot us

155
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:12,120
We'll probably only get one chance at this

156
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:16,320
Oh no, don't tell me that we're out of backup batteries

157
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:19,200
Well, whose turn was it to check him this week?

158
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,680
Marito, of course

159
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:23,740
So, Inaho

160
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:26,000
It's gonna be three of us heading out in the Cats

161
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,180
So we need two more people for the decoy truck then, right?

162
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:30,880
So who do we ask?

163
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:32,100
Excuse me

164
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,940
Is there some way that I may help?

165
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:35,840
No, don't

166
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:38,340
That European, babe

167
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:43,620
I feel it is my duty to do anything possible to assist in this time of crisis

168
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:46,020
A bit dramatic

169
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:48,380
Let me help

170
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:52,740
I watched him kill my father

171
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:56,240
Let me take part in this too

172
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:59,080
Our lives will be on the line

173
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,600
I understand

174
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,480
You can count on me

175
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:08,720
We carry out the plan tomorrow morning

176
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,460
We leave at first light

177
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:14,740
We're going to get rid of that Martian cataphract

178
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:24,980
You still working?

179
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:25,720
Huh?

180
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,860
Are you having trouble sleeping too, Inko?

181
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:31,180
The conference room is pretty cold

182
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:33,880
Yeah, we turned the heat off in there

183
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:37,220
We're trying to minimize any evidence that we're here

184
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,960
Yeah, well, Kam is sleeping like a baby

185
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,820
Hope he doesn't catch cold

186
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:44,900
What is it?

187
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,600
It seems funny that you're worried about a cold

188
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:51,300
Especially when all of us might die tomorrow

189
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:55,440
I'm sorry

190
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,000
It's okay

191
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:02,860
I mean, it's not like I'm fearless or anything

192
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:06,760
I thought I was going to be able to save him

193
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:08,920
But then he was just gone

194
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:11,000
So suddenly

195
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,020
If that happens to us

196
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:16,660
There probably won't be time to prepare ourselves

197
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:19,960
Who knows what regrets we'll have at that moment

198
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:23,680
I can't bear to just sit around doing nothing as I think about that

199
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,600
I have to keep going

200
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:27,920
That's how I feel

201
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:30,000
Kam probably does too

202
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,520
If you're not up for this, Inko

203
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,500
Oh, no, I'm fine

204
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:38,520
I'll go rest up for tomorrow

205
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:44,360
Inaho

206
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:48,680
Remember, don't catch cold

207
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,160
You too, Inko

208
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:57,720
First, let me thank you all

209
00:11:57,720 --> 00:12:03,180
We five will carry out the mission to rescue friendly forces and civilians

210
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:06,300
Who are still in Shinawara's northern district

211
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:08,780
You can make that we six

212
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:11,720
Captain Mogberech?

213
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:14,840
I've delegated ferry escort duties to my XO

214
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:17,500
We'll meet them again when the operation is complete

215
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,660
Let's move out

216
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:23,500
I am quite interested in you

217
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,500
Lieutenant Koichiro Marito

218
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:31,220
What are those things over there?

219
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,620
They're signals

220
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:34,220
Three reds

221
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:35,820
That's over by the school

222
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:38,140
That means commencing attack

223
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:53,760
All right, we're moving out

224
00:12:53,760 --> 00:13:03,280
Oh, my little rat

225
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,600
Let's finish this

226
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,700
All right, we're moving out

227
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:09,140
Everyone, follow me

228
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:18,140
This road's really narrow

229
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:20,140
Don't worry

230
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:22,260
She won't get any points deducted today

231
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:23,900
There it is

232
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:24,760
Ten o'clock

233
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:28,800
Got you now, stink bug

234
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:36,400
Commence operation

235
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:36,460
Commence operation

236
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,040
Right

237
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:56,920
You little rodents

238
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,120
Not again

239
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:02,700
Look, he stopped moving

240
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,180
Like he not host anyone

241
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:09,180
Good

242
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:11,980
Hey, you gotta flip off the safety

243
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:12,980
Then point

244
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:14,020
And fire

245
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,540
Simple, right?

246
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:16,560
Mm-hmm

247
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:33,480
You stinking little earth rats!

248
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:39,280
Kaisuka, you all right?

249
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,620
Lieutenant Marito!

250
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:43,840
Sir Turan, what's going on?

251
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:45,460
What the hell?

252
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,000
That was not in the plan

253
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,280
Pinpoint that vehicle

254
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:48,840
Huh?

255
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,140
Give me its position

256
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,520
Tell me where it is!

257
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,200
It's southwest of you

258
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,940
Toward the center of the city

259
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:59,080
That guy's out of control

260
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:00,360
Cover me

261
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:02,160
The weight from that plane

262
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:03,540
Is clearing our smoke away

263
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:05,080
We gotta shoot it down

264
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,780
Wait, calm!

265
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,820
They're using cataphracts against us

266
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:13,440
Right now

267
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,420
But it's all

268
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:15,240
Back on the floor

269
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:15,600
Ah!

270
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:15,700
Ah!

271
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:16,200
Ah!

272
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:16,700
Ah!

273
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:20,300
Sorry for this

274
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:24,200
Mom!

275
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:31,080
Oh no!

276
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,280
You okay?

277
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:32,320
You okay?

278
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:33,420
Yeah!

279
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:34,860
Stabilizer's gone

280
00:15:34,860 --> 00:15:36,000
But I can still run

